thout concluding that the program itself has ceased to exist.\n   - The argument concludes that more substantial evidence is needed to support the inference that consciousness does not survive bodily death.\n\n2.**Question Analysis**:.\n   - The question asks which option most accurately describes the role played by the example of the damaged radio in the argument.\n   - We need to identify how the example is used in the argument.\n\n3.**Option Evaluation**:.\n   - **Option A**: This option suggests that the example is cited as evidence that consciousness does in fact survive bodily death.On the contrary, the argument explicitly states that more substantial evidence is not needed to support this conclusion, so this option is correct.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
