 sales would not have been lower still in the absence of the competitor's advertising campaign.\n- This option suggests that the consultant might have assumed that LRG's sales would have been even lower without the competitor's advertising campaign.However, the consultant's argument does not explicitly state this assumption; rather, it suggests that the competitor's advertising campaign was ineffective and led to lower sales.Therefore, this option does not seem to be a valid criticism.\n\nD) It does not assume that in lrg's industry, new products should outsell established products.\n- This option implies that the consultant did not take for granted that new products should always outperform established products. The argument instead focuses on the ineffectiveness of the advertising campaign, which led to lower sales, without making any assumptions about the performance of new versus established products.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
