messages:  [["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe words we follow today to talk about ancient Chinese painting are all written by Chinese literati, and because of this, Chinese literati have dominated the discussion space of painting for a long time, and they have become accustomed to starting from their own point of view. choose a point of view that is good for literati and artists, and now-- or should have been-- it's time for us to compete with them. And we should also question what they call a good painter or good work. Many excellent non-literati artists do not get due recognition because of the prejudice of literati. Here, we should give them objective evaluation and due status one by one.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following statements is consistent with the original text?\n# Options:\nA) The appreciation level of literati artists lags behind their creative level\nB) In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice\nC) The literati have been in a strong position in the field of chinese painting theory for a long time\nD) The difference of interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting has a long history", "<think>.\nTo determine which statement is consistent with the original text, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) The appreciation level of literati artists lags behind their creative level.\n- The text does not mention anything about the appreciation level of literati artists lagging behind their creative level.It only discusses the dominance of literati in the discussion space of painting and the need for non-literati artists to be recognized.\n\nB) In ancient times, many talented literati and artists were buried because of prejudice.\n- The text does not provide any information about talented literati and artists being buried due to prejudice in ancient times.It only mentions that many talented non-literati artists do not get due recognition.\n\nThe text reveals that the difference of interest between ancient literati painting and non-literati painting does not have a long history, contradicting the idea that it has been a longstanding issue.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
