messages:   30%|###       | 183/600 [10:22<36:40,  5.28s/it][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nLaser technology is a high and new technology developed in the early 1960 s. The emission ability of the laser is strong and the energy is highly concentrated, which is hundreds of millions of times brighter than the ordinary light source and tens of billions times brighter than the sun's surface. If a medium-intensity laser beam is converged, a high temperature of thousands to tens of thousands of degrees can be produced in the focus. In addition, the monochromaticity of laser is very good. We know that different colors of light are determined by different wavelengths of light, while the wavelength of the laser is basically the same, the spectral line width is very narrow and the color is very pure. Because of this characteristic, laser is widely used in communication technology.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options is not conforming to the meaning of the text?\n# Options:\nA) Laser technology has a history of more than half a century\nB) The laser wavelength is basically the same and the monochromaticity is good\nC) Laser technology has a broad application prospect of science and technology\nD) Laser technology has the potential to subvert the traditional optical theory", "<think>.\nTo determine which option does not conform to the meaning of the text, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) Laser technology has a history of more than half a century.\n- The text states that laser technology was developed in the early 1960s.This means it has indeed been around for more than half a century.Therefore, this option conforms to the meaning of the text.\n\nB) The laser wavelength is basically the same and the monochromaticity is good.\n- The text mentions that the wavelength of the laser is basically the same and the monochromaticity is very good.This statement aligns with the information provided in the text.Therefore, this option conforms to the meaning of the text.\n\nD) Laser technology does not have the potential to subvert the traditional optical theory.\n- The text mentions laser technology's strong emission ability, high energy concentration, and monochromaticity, which align with traditional optical theories.This implies that laser technology does not have the potential to subvert the traditional optical theory.Therefore, this option contradicts the meaning of the text.\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
