tate that parents believe lying is the most unforgivable moral problem.Therefore, this option cannot be confirmed as true based on the given information.\n\nChildren\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not gone unnoticed by parents.\n- The context states that "the issue of children concealing their own situation from their parents is not only exacerbated, but also overlooked," suggesting that children\'s behavior of concealing their own situation has not gone unnoticed by parents.Therefore, this option cannot be confirmed as true based on the given information.\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
