messages:   34%|###4      | 205/600 [10:36<02:33,  2.58it/s][["Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAccording to the role of learning in the formation and development of mobility, human motivation can be divided into primitive motivation and acquisition motivation. Primitive motives are innate motives, which are based on people's instinctive needs; Acquisition motivation refers to all kinds of acquired motivation, that is, all kinds of motivation generated and developed through learning.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which of the following options is most likely to belong to the original motivation?\n# Options:\nA) Respect the elderly and parents\nB) Beautiful and gentle girls are loved by boys\nC) Nothing venture,nothing gain\nD) Respect teachers and education, respect literature and martial arts", "<think>.\nTo determine which option is most likely to belong to the original motivation, we need to consider the definition provided and analyze each option based on its nature.\n\nThe definition states that primitive motives are innate motives, which are based on people's instinctive needs.This means that these motives are inherent and not learned through experience or education.\n\nLet's examine each option:.\n\nA) Respect the elderly and parents - This is a learned behavior that is taught and reinforced through socialization and cultural norms.It is an innate instinctive need.\n\nB) Ugly and rough girls are hated by boys - This is a learned behavior that is based on societal expectations and preferences.It is an innate instinctive need.\n\nC) Everything venture, everything lose - This is a proverb that discourages taking risks and pursuing opportunities. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
