s, so this option seems less likely to be the primary vulnerability.\n\nB) Overlooks the possibility that a new computer model is liable to malfunction for reasons other than a microprocessor flaw: This option implies that the spokesperson might be assuming that all malfunctions are due to microprocessor flaws, without considering other potential causes.This could be a valid criticism, as it highlights the lack of evidence supporting the claim that microprocessor flaws are the only cause of malfunctions.Dismisses the possibility that the company mentioned adheres to industry-standard quality-control procedures without any evidence: This option implies that the spokesperson is disregarding the idea that the company follows standard quality-control procedures used by other companies.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
