messages:   48%|####7     | 285/600 [11:09<02:15,  2.33it/s][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nBroken window effect is a psychological phenomenon, that is, if the window of a house is broken and no one repair it, and soon other windows will also be broken.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, according to the above definition, which one of the followings does not belong to broken window effect?\n# Options:\nA) If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\nB) If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\nC) Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\nD) If a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are not stopped, many people will soon speak uncivilized languages.', "<think>.\nTo determine which option does not belong to the broken window effect, let's analyze each option based on the definition provided:.\n\n1.**Option A**: If the graffiti on a wall is not cleaned, the wall will soon be full of messy and ugly things.\n   - This option describes a situation where one act (not cleaning graffiti) leads to a chain reaction (more graffiti appearing).This aligns with the broken window effect, as it shows how one small act can lead to a larger problem if not addressed.\n\n2.**Option B**: If a tributary is polluted and not treated, it may pollute the water quality of the whole basin.\n   - This option describes a situation where one source of pollution (a tributary) can affect the entire basin if not treated.This also aligns with the broken window effect, as it shows how one small act (not treating pollution) can lead to a larger problem (polluting the entire basin).\n\n3.**Option C**: Once there is rubbish in a very clean place, people will throw their rubbish away without hesitation and will not feel ashamed.\n   - This option describes a situation where the presence of rubbish in a clean place leads to a change in behavior (people throwing rubbish without hesitation).This aligns with the broken window effect, as it shows how one small act (presence of rubbish) can lead to a change in behavior.\nIf a few people in a group speak uncivilized languages and are stopped, many people will not soon speak uncivilized languages.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
