ockage of arterioles deteriorates blood circulation in the head and neck, causing creases in the earlobe and increasing the risk of stroke.\n- This option provides a plausible mechanism for how the crease on the earlobe might be related to stroke risk.It suggests that blockage of arterioles leads to creases in the earlobe and increases the risk of stroke.This option directly supports the conclusion that the crease on the earlobe is a risk factor for stroke.\nCreases in the earlobe are not associated with any increased risk of diabetes, hypertension, ischemic heart disease, or peripheral vascular disease.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
