pply of black tea exceeds the demand.Therefore, we cannot confirm this statement based on the given information.\n\nB) The price of Indian green tea is higher than the international average price of green tea.\n- The text states that "the quality of green tea in India, Indonesia, and Sri Lanka, the main tea producing countries, is not high."This suggests that the price of Indian green tea might not necessarily be higher than the international average price of green tea.Therefore, we cannot confirm this statement based on the given information.\n\nThere is no trend of change red to green in the international tea market.\n- The text states that "since the 1970s, the above three countries began to change red to green in an attempt to occupy the international green tea market, all of which ended in failure."This suggests that there is a trend of change red to green in the international tea market.Therefore, this statement is consistent with the original text\n. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
