wn passwords makes it easier for others to gain unauthorized access.The context mentions that passwords are automatically locked after a certain number of incorrect guesses, making it difficult for attackers to gain access through brute force.Writing down passwords does not directly increase the risk of unauthorized access; instead, it might make it easier for the user to remember their password.Thus, this option is not strongly supported by the given information.\n\nC) **Complexity increases the likelihood of forgetting passwords**: This option suggests that complex passwords make it harder for users to remember them.The context provides information about the relationship between password complexity and user memory.Therefore, this option is supported by the given information.\n\nD) **Using complex passwords makes it easier to remember them**: This option suggests that using complex passwords can make it easier for users to remember them.The context provides information about the effectiveness of using complex passwords in remembering them.Therefore, this option is supported by the given information.\n\nBased on the analysis, all of the options are strongly supported by the given information.However, if we had to choose the option that is most likely to be contradicted by the given information, option B would be the worst choice\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
