messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B, C or D. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nFor example, X X Group held an anniversary celebration, your mobile phone number won a grand prize of 100000 yuan. this kind of unwise fraudulent text messages on mobile phones still appear again and again even after they have been exposed by the media. Professional swindlers prefer to use shoddy fraudulent text messages rather than design more deceptive and gullible text messages, which only shows that the swindlers are too stupid and unprofessional.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, which of the following options, if true, strongly refutes the above conclusion?\n# Options:\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\nC) If a deception was useless, the swindler would have eliminated it long ago.\nD) Swindlers use such text messages to catch people who may be fooled, and they want to filter out smart people in the first place.', "<think>.\nTo determine which option strongly refutes the conclusion, let's analyze each option step by step:.\n\nA) A swindler must be smart, otherwise it is impossible to deceive others.\n- This statement suggests that swindlers need to be smart to deceive others.However, it does not directly address the issue of why swindlers might use shoddy fraudulent text messages instead of more deceptive ones.Therefore, this option does not strongly refute the conclusion.\n\nB) When swindlers cheat, they will try their best not to attract the attention of the police.\n- This statement implies that swindlers are cautious about drawing attention to themselves.While this might be true, it does not directly address the reason why swindlers might use shoddy fraudulent text messages instead of more deceptive ones.Therefore, this option does not strongly refute the conclusion.\n\nD) Swindlers don't use such text messages to catch people who may be fooled, and they don't want to filter out smart people in the first place.\n- This statement implies that swindlers have no interest in targeting people who might be fooled and have no intention of filtering out smart individuals. This does not directly address the reason why swindlers might use shoddy fraudulent text messages instead of more deceptive ones. Therefore, this option does not strongly refute the conclusion.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
