t meet their expectations.\n- This option suggests that returnees might not be satisfied with their salaries, which could affect their job search.However, it does not directly explain why they struggle to find employment.It might not be a contributing factor and could be the primary reason.\n\nD) Graduates of famous overseas universities such as Oxford are not favored by employers.\n- This option suggests that employers do not prefer graduates from prestigious universities.While this might be true, it does not directly explain why returnees struggle to find employment.It is a separate factor that might affect the job market but may not be the primary reason for the phenomenon described.\n\nBased on the analysis, option B) Most returnees are familiar with the domestic employment situation and enterprise needs.This option best explains the phenomenon described in the context because it directly addresses why returnees might struggle to find employment after returning to China\n. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
