would weaken the argument that the bioengineered cotton is being overwhelmed by corn-bred bollworms.\n\nB) Whether corn could be bioengineered to produce the insecticide.\n- This option would provide information about the possibility of developing a bioengineered corn that produces the same insecticide as the bioengineered cotton.If such a bioengineered corn were developed, it would support the argument that the bioengineered cotton is being overwhelmed by corn-bred bollworms.\n\nC) Whether there are insecticides that can be used against bollworms that have developed resistance to the insecticide produced by the bioengineered cotton.Option B would not be helpful in evaluating the argument because it does not provide relevant information about the potential impact of alternative insecticides on controlling bollworms in bioengineered cotton.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
