      "text": " A) After hearing the tsunami warning, the tourists on the beach quickly evacuated to a higher place.\n\n2.**Option B**: \"When Li Ping took the exam, he brought two pencils as a precaution.\"This action demonstrates a proactive approach to managing potential risks (failing the exam) by taking preventive measures (bringing extra pencils). This aligns with the concept of crisis management planning as it involves anticipating and preparing for potential risks.. Therefore, my final option is:  B) When Li Ping took the exam, he brought two pencils as a precaution.\n\n3.**Option C**: \"Faced with a sudden earthquake, Xiao Zhang was knocked to the ground and fortunately escaped.\"This inaction showcases a reactive response to an actual crisis (earthquake) by neglecting preventive measures (remaining in a safe position). This contradicts the concept of crisis management planning as it disregards anticipating and preparing for potential risks.. Therefore, my final option is:  C) Faced with a sudden earthquake, Xiao Zhang was knocked to the ground and fortunately escaped.\n\n4.**Option D**: \"A company filed a bankruptcy application to the court due to heavy debts and unable to pay off its due debts.\"This action demonstrates a reactive response to an actual crisis (bankruptcy) by taking preventive measures (filing for bankruptcy). This aligns with the concept of crisis management planning as it involves anticipating and preparing for potential risks.. Therefore, my final option is:  D) A company filed a bankruptcy application to the court due to heavy debts and unable to pay off its due debts.\n</think>\n<answer>\nA) After hearing the tsunami warning, the tourists on the beach quickly evacuated to a higher place.\n</answer>",
