ere accidents, which might explain why the number of traffic deaths remains the same.This option helps resolve the discrepancy by providing another plausible explanation for the observed data.\n\n**Option C:** "In the last two years, most of the people killed in car accidents in the city were not wearing seat belts."\n- If most of the people killed in car accidents were not wearing seat belts, it would suggest that the seat belt laws are not effective in reducing fatalities.This option helps resolve the discrepancy by providing evidence that the laws are not working as intended.The seat belt laws have not had any impact on the city\'s automobile traffic patterns since their implementation.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
