nformation about multiple visits, so this option is not directly supported by the given information.\n\n4.**Option B**: This option claims that the residents of Groverhill have an unusually high occurrence of severe headaches.The context does not provide any information about the prevalence of severe headaches in Groverhill, so this option is not supported by the given information.\n\n5.The argument fails to overlook the possibility that residents of Groverhill visited their physicians more than once during the year for the same condition. This is because the number of consultations (105) is not significantly higher than the number of reported cases (35), which could not be due to multiple visits.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
