 on its main components.It only provides a criterion for determining unnaturalness but does not provide a clear justification for why nylon should be considered natural or not.\n\nA substance is no more natural than the processes used in its production.\nThis statement implies that the naturalness of a substance is limited by the naturalness of the processes involved in its production. This provides a clear criterion for evaluating the naturalness of nylon based on its production methods.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
