f agricultural openness.\n   - The domestic market and international market are becoming more integrated.\n   - The degree of agricultural openness will continue to improve.\n   - China faces competition from both developed and developing countries.\n   - Domestic agricultural products face challenges due to rising production costs, lack of price advantages, and increasing imports.\n   - The production of domestic agricultural products will face a double squeeze of price ceiling and cost floor, leading to a narrowing of the space for domestic price increases.\n\n2.**Question Analysis**:.\n   - The question asks for the main content of the text based on the given information.\n\n3.**Identifying the Main Content**:.The text primarily focuses on specific actions like improving market competitiveness, transforming the mode of agricultural development, being cautious about increasing agricultural openness, or solving the development dilemma of domestic agricultural products, rather than just discussing the challenges and strategies to address them.. Therefore, my final option is: "]]
